refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
boolsocket_getsockname Socketsocket stringaddress intport&null;
socket_getsockname should not be used with AF_UNIX sockets created with socket_connect: the name of a socket that is not bound is an empty string.

&reftitle.returnvalues;


 &return.success; &false; is returned when the underlying call fails, and the last socket
 error code is updated.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.5.0

     Now retrieves the interface index and its string representation when
     used on an AF_PACKET family socket.


   &sockets.changelog.socket-param;


    8.0.0

     A ValueError is now thrown when the socket family is not supported;
     previously an E_WARNING was emitted and &false; was returned.
